    <string name="accessibility_disclosure_body">Chime uses Android Accessibility to detect the package name of the app in the foreground and show a pause for apps you classify as distracting. Chime does not read screen text or keystrokes, take screenshots, or send this information off your device. You can disable this at any time in Android Settings under Accessibility.</string>
