    <string name="digest_consent_title">Before enabling notification access</string>
    <string name="digest_consent_access_details">Android grants the Chime notification listener technical access to the full notification object from every app, including title and text. Chime checks the originating package, ongoing and group-summary flags, category, media-session presence, default dialer/SMS identity, your allow-list, app classification, focus-mode suppression, and digest setting. Chime reads title and text only after the exclusions have passed and the app is classified as Distracting with batching active. Ignored notifications are not stored.</string>
    <string name="digest_consent_storage_details">Eligible notification titles and text are stored only in Chime\'s on-device database. Chime does not send notification content over the network.</string>
    <string name="digest_consent_turn_off_details">Turn batching off here, or revoke Chime under Android Settings &gt; Notification access. Revoking access stops the listener.</string>
